NNAAMMEE
     zznneeww — convert compressed files to gzipped files

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     zznneeww [--99ffKKttvv] _f_i_l_e _._._.

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The zznneeww utility uncompresses files compressed by compress(1) and recom‐
     presses them with gzip(1).

     The options are as follows:

     --99      Use the -9 mode of gzip(1), achieving better compression at the
             cost of slower execution.

     --ff      Overwrite existing ‘.gz’ files.  Unless this option is specified,
             zznneeww refuses to overwrite existing files.

     --KK      Keep the original ‘.Z’ file if it uses less disk blocks than the
             gzipped one.  A disk block is 1024 bytes.

     --tt      Test integrity of the gzipped file before deleting the original
             file.  If the integrity check fails, the original ‘.Z’ file is
             not removed.

     --vv      Print a report specifying the achieved compression ratios.

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     compress(1), gzip(1)

CCAAVVEEAATTSS
     The zznneeww utility tries to maintain the file mode of the original file.
     If the original file is not writable, it will be unable to do so and zznneeww
     will print a warning.

